        "_postman_id": "c7e52b8f-3d4a-5f69-a1b2-202610270002",
        "name": "Waai Media - Clients Management API",
        "description": "Postman Collection (v2.1) for the Waai Media Clients Management module.\n\n### 1. Environment\nImport `docs/Waai_Media_Local.postman_environment.json` and select it. This collection reuses its variables: `base_url`, `admin_email`, `admin_password`, `editor_email`, `editor_password`, `admin_token`, `editor_token`. Nothing is hardcoded here.\n\n### 2. Tokens\nAuthenticate via the Authentication collection or manually copy Bearer access tokens for Admin and Editor roles into the environment variables `admin_token` and `editor_token`.\n\n### 3. File Uploads\nFor multipart upload requests (e.g. Create Client, Replace Logo, Update Name & Logo), you MUST select a local image file (JPEG, PNG, or WebP up to 5 MB) in Postman's Body form-data tab under the `logo` key.\nNote on PHP limits: ensure `upload_max_filesize` and `post_max_size` in php.ini are at least 8M for reliable 5MB uploads.\n\n### 4. Roles\n- Super Admin & Admin: List, Show, Create, Update, Delete.\n- Editor: List, Show, Create, Update.\n- Editor DELETE requests return HTTP 403.\n- Unauthenticated admin requests return HTTP 401.\n- Public requests require no authentication.",
        "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
    },
